    <description>Screen subflow used to complete an asset return, exchange, or retirement.
Captures return details, creates Returned, Exchanged, or Retired Asset Assignment records, and updates the Asset status and current assignment.

-Add Pending Return to all Child assets
-Update to use Asset Assignment Subflows

2026-08-03: INC3-91 Phase 6 - The Retire Asset branch no longer creates Asset_Assignment__c via the legacy shared writer (Asset_Assignment_Subflow_Autolaunched_Update_Status_Assigments_Flow_1 removed - it has no other callers left in this org). Set_Retire_Vals now also stamps Get_Asset.Retirement_Date__c / Retirement_Reason__c directly (mirrored onto Asset in Phase 0) and computedNotes (via new retireNotes formula, folding in Retire_Notes__c). A new Update_Retired_Asset record update stamps Status=&quot;Retired&quot; + Status_Change_Notes__c + Retirement_Date__c/Retirement_Reason__c on the Asset, triggering Asset_After_Create_Assignment_on_Status_Change to create the assignment and stamp Current_Assignment__c. Note: the legacy writer&#39;s inputAssetCollection on the Retire path always referenced Find_Children, which the Retire branch never actually populates (that lookup only runs on the Return branch) - so Retire never created assignments for child assets before this change either; behavior for children is unchanged (still asset-only). Find_Children itself is untouched/still required by the Return branch&#39;s Single_or_Multi_Return decision. assignmentToCreate.Retirement_Date__c/Retirement_Reason__c/Retire_Notes__c assignments in Set_Retire_Vals are now vestigial but left in place to minimize diff.</description>
